{"seq":4,"slug":"major-works","title":"亚里士多德·major-works","stage":"DONE","category":"aristotle","categoryLabel":"亚里士多德","chapterCount":3,"docCount":6,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/major-works","rating":{"composite":3.78,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":4,"strategic":4.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/famous-people/23_aristotle/4_major-works","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"亚里士多德-主要著作\">亚里士多德·主要著作</h1><p>亚里士多德传世的著作（Corpus Aristotelicum 共 45 部论著，多为吕克昂学园的内部讲稿）是一座百科全书式的知识宝库，覆盖逻辑、形而上学、伦理、政治、自然科学与文艺理论。本 hub 以**&quot;著作本身&quot;为单位**考察其代表作：它们的文本结构、篇目构成、编纂与传抄命运、Bekker 标准页码定位，以及作为一部部&quot;书&quot;在两千余年里的传承。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本-hub-vs-兄弟-hub-的分工\">本 hub vs 兄弟 hub 的分工</h2><p>本 hub（4·主要著作）回答&quot;<strong>这些是什么书、如何成书、如何流传</strong>&quot;，刻意与兄弟 hub 分工、不重复其内容：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><a href=\"../ideas-and-methods/\">3·思想与方法</a></strong> 讲学说的<strong>思想内容</strong>（实体与形式、四因说、中道、潜能与现实）——本 hub 谈承载这些学说的&quot;书&quot;，思想细节交叉链接过去。</li>\n<li><strong><a href=\"../core-contributions/\">2·核心贡献</a></strong> 讲他<strong>开创了哪些学科</strong>（逻辑之父、生物学之父）——本 hub 谈这些贡献沉淀成的具体著作。</li>\n<li><strong><a href=\"../life-and-times/\">1·生平与时代</a></strong> 讲其生平（医生之子、吕克昂学园）——这是著作产生的背景。</li>\n<li><strong><a href=\"../influence-and-legacy/\">5·影响与遗产</a></strong> 与 <strong><a href=\"../controversies-and-appraisal/\">6·争议与评价</a></strong> 讲著作的后世影响与功过——本 hub 谈著作本身、影响细节链接过去。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"六篇与推荐学习路径\">六篇与推荐学习路径</h2><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>章节</th>\n<th>篇目</th>\n<th>看点</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>逻辑与形而上学</td>\n<td><a href=\"logic-and-metaphysics/the-organon-works\">《工具论》诸篇</a></td>\n<td>六部逻辑论著、Bekker 定位、编纂史</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>逻辑与形而上学</td>\n<td><a href=\"logic-and-metaphysics/the-metaphysics-work\">《形而上学》</a></td>\n<td>书名由来、14 卷异质结构、两个&quot;第一卷&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>伦理与政治</td>\n<td><a href=\"ethics-and-politics/the-nicomachean-ethics\">《尼各马可伦理学》</a></td>\n<td>家族命名、10 卷结构、当代德性伦理复兴</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>伦理与政治</td>\n<td><a href=\"ethics-and-politics/the-politics-work\">《政治学》</a></td>\n<td>158 部城邦宪法、《雅典政制》失而复得</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>科学与艺术</td>\n<td><a href=\"science-and-art/the-natural-works\">自然科学著作</a></td>\n<td>物理学之误 vs 生物学之辉煌</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>科学与艺术</td>\n<td><a href=\"science-and-art/the-poetics\">《诗学》</a></td>\n<td>残本、悲剧六要素、卡塔西斯、三一律之误读</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>前置知识</strong>：建议先读 <a href=\"../life-and-times/tutor-and-the-lyceum/founding-the-lyceum\">生平·吕克昂的创立</a> 了解著作产生的学园背景。<strong>推荐路径</strong>：逻辑（《工具论》是一切研究的工具）→ 形而上学（第一哲学）→ 伦理与政治（实践科学）→ 自然科学与诗学。读毕可转入 <a href=\"../ideas-and-methods/\">3·思想与方法</a> 深入学说内涵，或 <a href=\"../controversies-and-appraisal/\">6·争议与评价</a> 审视其功过。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"logic-and-metaphysics","title":"Logic And Metaphysics","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/major-works/logic-and-metaphysics","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-organon-works","title":"《工具论》诸篇","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/major-works/logic-and-metaphysics/the-organon-works"},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-metaphysics-work","title":"《形而上学》","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/major-works/logic-and-metaphysics/the-metaphysics-work"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"ethics-and-politics","title":"Ethics And Politics","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/major-works/ethics-and-politics","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-nicomachean-ethics","title":"《尼各马可伦理学》","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/major-works/ethics-and-politics/the-nicomachean-ethics"},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-politics-work","title":"《政治学》","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/major-works/ethics-and-politics/the-politics-work"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"science-and-art","title":"Science And Art","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/major-works/science-and-art","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-natural-works","title":"自然科学著作","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/major-works/science-and-art/the-natural-works"},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-poetics","title":"《诗学》","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/aristotle/major-works/science-and-art/the-poetics"}]}]}